  "body": "Track: P\n\nGuarded scalar loops can now pass their actual normal BREAK result to an outer source binding, ordinary Copy, and an existing pure known-direct usize-to-u8 predicate. The generated C uses the runtime exit value; it does not replace the result with an expected literal.\n\nThe bounded family has one usize carry slot, a literal initial value and guard/step, one static CONTINUE and one normal BREAK. ADD and SUB preserve the existing all-header-state representability conditions. The private result bridge authenticates the real source/target/operand and exact post-frame, then creates a free Unknown Copy package in the caller world. It does not import another world's value IDs or publish a known-number receipt. Existing size/offset quantity consumers stay known-only; the new Unknown route is explicit for ordinary binding/Copy and the existing predicate actual.\n\nProduction changes are limited to four private files. They reuse the existing three graph/seven world seals, add no snapshots, and leave NLStutterProof at 3256 bytes on the measured GCC build. Public API/ABI/issuer, canonical semantics, toolchain and workflows are unchanged.\n\nValidation on retained candidate 2f1f34e:\n\n- Five independent positive sources cover zero/one/multiple backedges, overshoot, ADD/SUB, and different exit values and source decisions. Five negative sources retain rejection/no-clobber.\n- GCC Debug: 671/671 CTest PASS. Strict C17 native: 40 observations across GCC/Clang O0/O2 and unmodified/passively observed C. Optimized GCC host also passed the new current/native cohort.\n- ADD/SUB each reached registration592, invocation608 and named1280 OOM positions: 4960 total, with status, rollback, no-publication, current retry and named-output bytes/inode/mtime/temp preservation.\n- ASan/LSan and UBSan: the five new current/OOM/native gates passed. Old stuttering current and eight-source native/negative/golden-byte cohorts passed under both sanitizers. This is targeted sanitizer coverage, not a claim of all 671 tests under sanitizers.\n- Source/result/target/type/current/dependency mutations and canonical ownership cases passed. The ending-loan source is rejected earlier at arithmetic precision, so it is not evidence of reaching the loan barrier.\n\nAll source/oracle/harness freezes, FIRST/RED and earlier candidate results are retained. Prospective v35 pins v34 by external SHA/Git blob and inherits 3338 protected inputs; v1-v34 and old evidence are unchanged. See the [local evidence and limits](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1139#issuecomment-6621031466).\n\nPublication history:\n\n- C224 ordinary merge 070209f has parents 2f1f34e + adopted main63009b8 and exactly the retained tree e6f12538967d18e046b26ac69ba2f5a0bfd9300d.\n- Publication HEAD 773643d additionally forward-merges the approved Roadmap-only main acdbf91; its tree is 3d230802ca275bd963101c9b575f1567927f5c7a. Production/tests are byte-identical to the local tested candidate.\n- Integration history/protocol checks and format pass. [C224 integration receipts](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1139#issuecomment-6622170956).\n- First natural CI pair is all-green: [FULL5 41770800325](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/actions/runs/41770800325), each 674/674; [NO-LLVM PARTIAL 41770800106](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/actions/runs/41770800106), 673/673 plus the downstream real CLI check. Both attempt1, 6 actual jobs total, manual0. All six decoded job logs confirm checkout 7394f748ff019f3f42da1c3fe4e85f12ba559948 (tree identical to this HEAD), complete test counts, exit0 and no CTest skips. Additional push/CI stopped at this first reliable all-green.\n\nUnsupported or unverified: named usize returns, general root IF/arithmetic consumers, T-changing/multiple/nested C/B, variable guards/steps, general range/termination and H-heap composition. Independent review of this new result/current/consumer change is pending Coordination assignment.\n\nVALUE-ALIGNMENT-RISK: source/owner/current/consumer audit and future coverage/history maintenance remain costs. Capability evidence does not establish general soundness or Product PASS; audit locality UNMEASURED / GO624 PAUSED / H1 HOLD.\n\nRefs #1139. DRAFT/HOLD for independent review; no READY, merge or Product GO. P1036/PR1050 STOP remains in force.",
